    {
      "id": "PRESETS.DEF",
      "display": "Prince of Persia 2 PRESETS.DEF",
      "description": "PRESETS.DEF of Prince of Persia 2 (DOS): the FM instruments. The DOS setup program copies the Sound Blaster Pro's instruments to this file, and on the install disks it is SNDDRVRS\\PRESET33.DEF. It is needed whatever plays the music, because the timing of the story scenes comes from the FM driver. You have to supply it. The package contains none of the game's data. A modified file of your own can be used instead, and the project records exactly which file it was.",
      "size": 2049,
      "sha1": "AE5547FB0D840EE0AB643FE41046A9289B28F310",
      "name": "PRESETS.DEF"
    },
    {
      "id": "PRINCE.EXE",
      "display": "Prince of Persia 2 1.0 PRINCE.EXE",
      "description": "PRINCE.EXE of Prince of Persia 2 1.0 (DOS): the program. SDLPoP2 reads its tables (the characters' animations, how the rooms are drawn and the text). You have to supply it. The package contains none of the game's data. A modified file of your own can be used instead, and the project records exactly which file it was. The file expected here is the program without a crack. A cracked copy plays the same, because only the copy protection's code differs and SDLPoP2 does not run that code.",
      "size": 292865,
      "sha1": "9BDBC04C4DA7443CDA8C4DACD5AD6ADD8BAEA228",
      "name": "PRINCE.EXE",
      "requiredWhen": {
        "setting": "version",
        "in": [
          "1.0"
        ]
      }
    },
